From 4daa457b2c610398ed70a651744e79637e3018e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shiro <build@shiro>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:22:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] emscripten: real fork() under Shiro (process snapshot
 restored in a new worker)

fork() and clone() without CLONE_VFORK snapshot the process: every mapped
page (reserved untouched pages as zero, file pages faulted in), the forking
thread's registers, the signal table, brk/automap and the ELF info. The
kernel makes the child (SYS_shiro_vfork), host.mjs hands the snapshot to the
page, which starts a new Blink worker that rebuilds it (ShiroRestore from
Exec) and runs with fork() returning 0. vfork and CLONE_VFORK keep the
emulation on the calling thread.
---
 blink/blink.c   |  10 ++
 blink/shiro.inc | 272 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 280 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

